<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <PropertyGroup>
    <TargetFrameworks>net48;net8.0;net9.0;net10.0</TargetFrameworks>
    <LangVersion>latest</LangVersion>
    <GeneratePackageOnBuild>true</GeneratePackageOnBuild>
    <Nullable>enable</Nullable>
    <Version>1.4.0</Version>
    <Authors>Hamed Afzali</Authors>
    <Company>PixelWizards</Company>
    <Description>HRpc - Event-driven messaging framework for .NET (TCP and local Named Pipes)</Description>
    <PackageProjectUrl>https://github.com/hamedafzali/HRpc</PackageProjectUrl>
    <RepositoryUrl>https://github.com/hamedafzali/HRpc</RepositoryUrl>
    <PackageTags>ipc;named-pipes;tcp;messaging;eventbus;duplex;desktop;dotnet;rpc;csharp</PackageTags>
    <PackageLicenseExpression>MIT</PackageLicenseExpression>
    <PackageReadmeFile>README.md</PackageReadmeFile>
    <!-- Shown on nuget.org's "Release Notes" tab and in Visual Studio's package manager.
         Plain text, not Markdown. Rewrite it for every release (see docs/RELEASING.md). -->
    <PackageReleaseNotes>1.4.0 - compatible with 1.3 in both directions; all new behavior is opt-in.

New:
- Server push: Server.SendAsync(clientId, message), BroadcastAsync(message), ConnectedClients.
- Client ids on server-side events and in the new RequestContext.
- Request cancellation: a timed-out or cancelled SendAndWaitAsync stops the handler on a 1.4 server (OnRequest overload with RequestContext.CancellationToken).
- MaxConcurrentRequests (default 1, as before) runs a client's requests in parallel.
- KeepAlive for TCP and CurrentUserOnly for named pipes.

Fixed:
- PipeServer busy-looped while idle, and could drop clients during connection bursts on Linux and macOS.
- Late replies to timed-out requests no longer show up as MessageReceived events.
- A throwing ClientConnected subscriber no longer stops a TcpServer accepting clients.

Full changelog: https://github.com/hamedafzali/HRpc/blob/main/CHANGELOG.md
Samples: https://github.com/hamedafzali/HRpc/blob/main/docs/SAMPLES.md</PackageReleaseNotes>
    <GenerateAssemblyInfo>false</GenerateAssemblyInfo>
    <!-- TODO: no PackageIcon set — no image file available yet. Once one is added
         (e.g. icon.png, 128x128), wire it up with <PackageIcon>icon.png</PackageIcon>
         plus a matching <None Include="icon.png" Pack="true" PackagePath="\" /> item. -->

    <!-- SourceLink / deterministic build. SourceLink itself is built into the .NET 8+ SDK
         (the old Microsoft.SourceLink.GitHub 8.0.0 package pulled in a vulnerable
         Microsoft.Build.Tasks.Git). -->
    <PublishRepositoryUrl>true</PublishRepositoryUrl>
    <EmbedUntrackedSources>true</EmbedUntrackedSources>
    <Deterministic>true</Deterministic>
    <ContinuousIntegrationBuild Condition="'$(GITHUB_ACTIONS)' == 'true'">true</ContinuousIntegrationBuild>

    <!-- Symbol package -->
    <IncludeSymbols>true</IncludeSymbols>
    <SymbolPackageFormat>snupkg</SymbolPackageFormat>
  </PropertyGroup>
  <ItemGroup>
    <None Include="README.md" Pack="true" PackagePath="\" />
    <Compile Remove="Tests\**\*.cs" />
    <Compile Remove="pipetemplate\**\*.cs" />
    <None Include="Tests\**\*" />
    <None Include="pipetemplate\**\*" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup Condition="'$(TargetFramework)' == 'net48'">
    <PackageReference Include="Newtonsoft.Json" Version="13.0.3" />
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>
